is_error":false,"num_turns":35,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I patched the network by feeding the east left-pocket readings (E2) into the weights of the dead west left-pocket inputs (W2). The three files are in `work/`, along with my scripts.\n\n**What I changed and why:** In 4 of the 6 recorded start-network runs, the junction gridlocked. West left-turners filled their 3-car pocket and backed up, blocking the west straight lane. The network couldn't see this and held phase 2 (EW_through) with nothing moving. East and west carry the same demand, and phase 3 empties both left pockets together, so E2 is the best stand-in for W2. I added the W2 weight columns onto the E2 columns (`W1[:,5] += W1[:,11]`, `W1[:,17] += W1[:,23]`). The network now behaves exactly as if the W2 readings equalled the E2 readings. Nothing was fitted.\n\n**Parameters changed:** 128 of 7428, confirmed with `tools.edit_size`.\n\n**Checks (forward passes only, no simulator):**\n- **Gridlock states:** in 2123 recorded states where the start network wrongly held phase 2, the patched network picks phase 3 in 2120.\n- **Wasted holds** (keeping a green with empty lanes while others queue): down from 2200 to 31.\n- **Proxy check on the north/south pockets,** where both detectors work: rebuilding one pocket from the other matched the true decision 87–93% of the time.\n- **Other proxies:** I also tried scaled-down estimates, but they did worse.\n\nI couldn't test the closed loop, so a leftover gridlock at high demand can't be ruled out. One such episode would add about 50 veh-h to the high mean.\n\n**Predicted test TTS:**\n\n| Scenario | Predicted (veh-h) |\n|---|---|\n| low | 35.5 |\n| nominal | 46.0 |\n| high | 58.0 |","ttft_ms":1056,"type":"result","duration_ms":618390,"uuid":"829a08dd-99c3-4906-9760-e0714456e9a0","ttft_stream_ms":907,"time_to_request_ms":60,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":2,"system_prompt":8,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":21,"input_hooks":1,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":3,"tool_pool_refresh":2,"init_message":2,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":0,"loop_entry":2,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":3,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":4,"message_normalization":1,"client_creation":0,"request_build":5},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":10,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":128,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"deferred_tools_delta","slowest_producer_ms":3,"cpu_ms":47,"major_faults":0,"setup_ms":0,"prompt_producers_ms":0,"ambient_start_ms":16,"ambient_wait_ms":2,"render_ms":0,"producers":43,"token_counts":0},"tool_schema_build_detail":{"betas_ms":0,"waits_ms":0,"placement_ms":1,"render_ms":2,"after_ms":0,"other_ms":1,"tools":14,"new_schemas":14},"message_normalization_detail":{"before_ms":0,"normalize_ms":1,"images_ms":0,"post_process_ms":0,"after_ms":0,"other_ms":0,"messages":12,"wire_messages":2},"request_build_detail":{"records_ms":0,"system_ms":0,"headers_ms":1,"cache_break_record_ms":0,"plans_ms":1,"retry_setup_ms":0,"sent_build_ms":0,"record_attempt_ms":2,"other_ms":1,"sent_build_safety_context_ms":0,"sent_build_cache_breakpoints_ms":0,"sent_build_surrogate_scan_ms":0},"first_content_frame_ms":908,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-12-02T07:15:00.587Z"}
